-- FitFast: dishes, desserts and drinks from the Department of Health table.
-- Source: ตารางแสดงคุณค่าทางโภชนาการของอาหารไทย 2561, สำนักโภชนาการ กรมอนามัย
--   https://nutrition2.anamai.moph.go.th/th/thai-food-composition-table
--   (scanned PDF; values transcribed from the one-plate dish, dessert/bakery
--   and miscellaneous sections and checked against 4P + 9F + 4C = energy).
-- Drinks are listed per bottle in the source and converted here to per 100 mL
-- (1 fl oz = 29.57 mL). The source has no sugar values, so sugar is empty.
-- Foods that already exist in Thai FCD are skipped; for desserts that already
-- exist only the DoH piece weight is added as a serving.
-- Run after food_search_names.sql and portion_setup_phase2.sql (needs their columns).
-- Safe to re-run.

-- The catalogue was first loaded with explicit ids, so the id counter can be
-- behind the highest id (error 23505 on foods_catalog_pkey). Move it forward.
select setval(pg_get_serial_sequence('public.foods_catalog', 'id'),
              (select coalesce(max(id), 1) from public.foods_catalog));

